  "job_B3.2.22_20251003_114621": {
    "text": "S\u00e6ge\u00f0 on \u00f0ysum bocum be \u00f0\u00e6re arwur\u00f0nysse \u00feyses halgan d\u00e6ges and be \u00f0\u00e6re unasecgendlican\nSwa he us \u00e6ghwylces godes bisne beforan onstealde, dyde he, swa se so\u00f0a lareow don sceolde.\nHe \u00e6ghw\u00e6\u00f0er ge he us mid his wordum l\u00e6rde, ge eac mid his bisenum beforan tacnode, hu we don\n\u00deonne w\u00e6s on \u00f0ysum d\u00e6ge, \u00fe\u00e6tte ure drihten \u00e6lmihtig god hine sylfne to \u00f0an geeadmedde, \u00fe\u00e6t he to\nHe drihten wolde \u00e6rest her on middaneard gebreman and geweor\u00f0ian \u00fea Iudeiscan \u00e6fter \u00fe\u00e6re wisan, \u00fee\nSceolon we \u00fe\u00e6t witan, \u00fe\u00e6tte se halga lichama ures drihtnes, \u00fee we nu on cirican \u00feicga\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00fe\u00e6t\nCum dilexisset suos, qui erant in mundo, He drihten lufode his \u00fea halgan, \u00fea \u00f0e on \u00f0ysum middanearde\nRihtlice \u00fe\u00e6t is gecweden, for\u00f0an \u00fee he \u00f0a lufan to \u00f0\u00e6s for\u00f0 wi\u00f0 heo gecydde, \u00fe\u00e6t he efne lichamlicne\n\u00dea gefylde he sylf \u00feone cwide, \u00fee he \u00e6r cw\u00e6\u00f0: Maiorem namque hac dilectione nemo habet, He cw\u00e6\u00f0:\nHw\u00e6t, he \u00feonne \u00fea lufan ure drihten swi\u00f0e healice wi\u00f0 eall mancyn gecydde, \u00fea he, swa ic \u00e6r s\u00e6de, se\nFor\u00f0an we sceolon nu \u00fe\u00e6re micclan lufan urum drihtne singallice \u00feancian, \u00e6ghw\u00e6\u00f0er ge mid wordum,\nIn festivitate Iudeorum facta est cena domini, On Iudea symbelnysse w\u00e6ron geworden drihtnes\nAnd se h\u00e6lend w\u00e6s hlionigende \u00e6t \u00f0am gereordum mid his apostolum and mid heom mete \u00feigde.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s se ealda feond his inwites and his facnes swi\u00f0e gemyndig.\nS\u00e6nde \u00fea hine sylfne on \u00f0\u00e6s mannes heortan, \u00fee Iudas w\u00e6s gehaten, and hine l\u00e6rde, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde\nW\u00e6s he \u00fees ilca Iudas \u00fea mid \u00feam h\u00e6lende \u00e6t \u00f0am gereordum.\nAnd he w\u00e6s \u00e6r on \u00f0\u00e6ra twelf apostola rim geteald, \u00e6r he \u00fea hine sylfne swi\u00f0e earme and unl\u00e6dlice of\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 se godspellere, \u00fe\u00e6t se deofol hit s\u00e6nde on \u00f0\u00e6s mannes heortan, \u00fee Iudas w\u00e6s gehaten.\nN\u00e6s na, \u00fe\u00e6t se feond him openlice utan to spr\u00e6ce \u00feurh earena gehyrnysse, ac his heortan and his\nAnd eall \u00fe\u00e6t se deofol \u00fe\u00e6r mynte manncynne to \u00f0am m\u00e6stan yfele gedon, eall \u00fe\u00e6t eft mancynne to\nSciens, quia omnia dedit ei pater in manu sua, He wiste, \u00fe\u00e6t him godf\u00e6der eall on his handa and on his\nEalle godcundlice gesceafta standa\u00f0 on drihtnes gewealdum, for\u00f0an \u00f0e he is se ilca god, se \u00f0e ealle\nEalle \u00feing he \u00e6tsamne gesih\u00f0 and sceawa\u00f0 and ealle \u00feing him beo\u00f0 opene and cu\u00f0e.\nNis \u00e6niges mannes modge\u00f0anc to \u00f0\u00e6s deagol, \u00fe\u00e6t hit him behyded sy.\nHe drihten \u00fe\u00e6t ongeat and geseah, \u00fe\u00e6t se deofol \u00feone Iudas l\u00e6rde, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine bel\u00e6wde.\nAc \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feeah hw\u00e6\u00f0ere ge\u00f0yldelice ab\u00e6r and gemetf\u00e6stlice scirde, for\u00f0an \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6t wiste, \u00fe\u00e6t hit\nWiste he, \u00fe\u00e6t he on his sylfes gewealdum and on his godcundre mihte h\u00e6fde \u00e6ghw\u00e6\u00f0er ge \u00f0one\nAnd eall \u00fe\u00e6t yfel and ealne \u00feone ni\u00f0, \u00fee heo wi\u00f0 hine gefremedon, eall he drihten \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feurh hine sylfne\nEt quia a Deo exivit et ad Deum vadit, And he wiste, \u00fe\u00e6t he fram godf\u00e6der on middaneard asended\nSo\u00f0lice \u00feeah \u00f0e he drihten us hider on middaneard eadmodlice gesohte on menniscne lichaman,\nAnd \u00feeah \u00f0e he eft of \u00f0ysum middanearde to godf\u00e6der on heofonas ferde, hw\u00e6\u00f0ere he her on worulde\nSurgit a cena et posuit vestimenta sua, He \u00f0a aras se h\u00e6lend, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea se godspellere, fram \u00feam\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he his hr\u00e6gl asette.\nHe m\u00e6nde, \u00fe\u00e6t he hit on anre stowe alede.\nMid \u00fey he getacnode, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde his \u00feone halgan lichaman on dea\u00f0 gesettan for ealles mancynnes\nHe hw\u00e6\u00f0ere eft \u00feone ilcan lichaman swi\u00f0e wlitigne and wundorlicne gefremede \u00feurh his \u00fea halgan\nEt cum accepisset linteum, praecinxit se.\nHe \u00f0a onfeng line and hine mid begyrde, \u00fe\u00e6t is, \u00fe\u00e6t he onfeng \u00fe\u00e6re m\u00e6stan streng\u00f0u, mid \u00fe\u00e6re he\nAnd we eac witan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t bi\u00f0 \u00feegnes riht, \u00feonne he wile teala \u00feenian, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine sceal to \u00f0an gyrdan\nTo \u00f0an se heofonlica cyning \u00e6lmihtig god us hider on middaneard gesohte on menniscum lichaman,\nDeinde misit aquam in pelvem, He \u00f0a het geotan w\u00e6ter on mundleow and ongan his \u00feegna fet \u00fewean\nHw\u00e6t, he drihten on \u00f0ysse d\u00e6de \u00fea his word and \u00feone his cwide f\u00e6gere gefylde, \u00fee he \u00e6r sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0:\nOn \u00f0\u00e6re eadmodlican bisene is \u00e6teowed, \u00fe\u00e6t men sceoldon him betweonon beon eadmode and \u00fe\u00e6tte\nVenit ergo ad Simonem Petrum, He \u00f0a com to his \u00f0egne, \u00fee Petrus w\u00e6s gehaten.\nN\u00e6s na, \u00fe\u00e6t he latost to him come, ac he ealra \u00e6rest to him eode, and he \u00e6rest \u00e6t him ongan heora fet\nGeearnode he \u00fey sy\u00f0\u00f0an, \u00fee he drihten heora ealra modge\u00f0ances cunnode and be him sylfum hi ealle\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Petrus him to andsware: Tu es Christus, filius Dei vivi, \u00feu eart Crist, \u00fe\u00e6s lifigendan godes\n\u00dea on \u00f0\u00e6re drihtenlican andetnysse geearnode he \u00feone ealdordom ealra godes ciricena and \u00fea c\u00e6gian\nHe drihten com to Petre, swa ic \u00e6r s\u00e6de and wolde his fet \u00fewean.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he Petrus to him: Hu m\u00e6g \u00fe\u00e6t, min drihten, swa beon, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu mine fet \u00fewea?\nEfne swa swa he cw\u00e6de: Ic eom \u00feurh mine tydderlice gecynd lichamlic man and \u00feu eart ece god ealra\nNis \u00fe\u00e6t for\u00f0an gedafenlic, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu to minum fotum onhnige.\nCw\u00e6\u00f0 he Crist to him: \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t ic her do, nast \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t geta, for hwan ic swa do; \u00feu hit \u00feonne wast\nHe drihten geseah forhtian \u00fe\u00e6s his \u00feegnes mod for his \u00fe\u00e6re eadmodlican \u00feenunge.\n\u00dea trymede he hine mid his \u00fea gewunelican arf\u00e6stnysse, \u00fe\u00e6t he ge\u00f0yldelice bidan sceolde, hw\u00e6nne he\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 him Petrus to: Non lavabis mihi pedes in aeternum, Min drihten, ne \u00fewehst \u00feu n\u00e6fre mine\nHe forhtade, swa ic \u00e6r cw\u00e6\u00f0, for \u00f0\u00e6re drihtnes eadmodnysse; \u00feuhte him \u00fe\u00e6t wundorlic and egeslic,\nSe man ana w\u00e6s, \u00fe\u00e6tte eadmodnysse wi\u00f0soc and hw\u00e6\u00f0ere for hyrsumnysse ge\u00f0afode.\nCw\u00e6\u00f0 him to se h\u00e6lend: Gif ic ne \u00fewea \u00feine fet, \u00feonne nafast \u00feu d\u00e6l mid me.\nOn \u00f0ysum is gecy\u00f0ed, \u00fe\u00e6t seo on\u00f0w\u00e6gennyss \u00fe\u00e6ra fota gastlice tacna\u00f0 gehw\u00e6\u00f0er ge lichaman\nDrihten, n\u00e6s na \u00fe\u00e6t an, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu mine fet \u00fewea, ac \u00feu eac \u00feweh mine handa and min heafod.\nEfne swa swa he cw\u00e6de: Nu \u00f0u, drihten, \u00feus egeslice beotast, \u00fe\u00e6t ic elles n\u00e6bbe d\u00e6l mid \u00fee, buton \u00feu\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he Crist to him: Se man, se \u00f0e a\u00few\u00e6gen bi\u00f0, ne bi\u00f0 him \u00fe\u00e6s \u00feearf, \u00fe\u00e6t hine man eft \u00fewea,\nHw\u00e6t m\u00e6nde he drihten on \u00f0am wordum?\nHw\u00e6t, we witan, \u00fe\u00e6t ne bi\u00f0 \u00e6nig man to \u00f0\u00e6s cl\u00e6ne a\u00f0w\u00e6gen, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fe\u00e6s hw\u00e6\u00f0ere n\u00e6bbe \u00feearfe, \u00fe\u00e6t\nAc he m\u00e6nde, swa ic \u00e6r cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fea gastlican on\u00few\u00e6gennysse, \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00fe\u00e6t halige fulwihtes b\u00e6\u00f0 and\nNe sceal hine man eft fulwian, ne \u00fe\u00e6t alefed nis.\nAc \u00fea synna and incan, \u00fee him sy\u00f0\u00f0an gelimpa\u00f0, \u00feonne sceal he \u00f0a \u00feurh cl\u00e6ne andetnysse and \u00feurh\nEt vos mundi estis, sed non omnes, and ge syndon cl\u00e6ne, cw\u00e6\u00f0 he Crist to \u00f0am his \u00feegnum, n\u00e6s na\nHer on \u00f0ysum cwide w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6ra apostola toscadennys.\nEalle hi w\u00e6ron cl\u00e6ne buton Iudas ana.\nHe w\u00e6s l\u00e6wa and myr\u00f0ra and fur\u00f0on he hine sylfne swi\u00f0e unl\u00e6dlice mid grine aheng and awyrigde\nFor\u00f0an he drihten \u00fe\u00e6t cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t hi ealle n\u00e6ron cl\u00e6ne, for\u00f0an \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6t geare wiste, hwylc heora \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00c6fter\u00fean \u00fee se h\u00e6lend \u00fea h\u00e6fde heora fet ge\u00fewagen, \u00fea onfeng he eft his hr\u00e6gle and hine mid\nOn \u00f0am w\u00e6s getacnod, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6fter\u00feam \u00fee he ure drihten for ealles mancynnes h\u00e6lu lichamlice dea\u00f0\nEt cum recubuisset iterum, dixit eis: Scitis, quid fecerim vobis, \u00fea se h\u00e6lend hine \u00fea gegered h\u00e6fde,\nIc wolde mid \u00feam gecy\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t ge \u00fe\u00e6t wisten, nu ic eowre fet \u00fewoh, \u00fee eower drihten and eower\nAnd ic eow \u00fe\u00e6t dyde to bisene, \u00fe\u00e6t ic me to \u00f0am geeadmette, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow nu mid eadmodnysse\nOn \u00f0ysum cwide us is openlice gecy\u00f0ed and \u00e6teowed, \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00fe\u00e6s habba\u00f0 miccle ned\u00feearfe, \u00fe\u00e6t we\n\u00de\u00e6t we sibbe and lufan and eadmodnysse us betweonan healden and \u00fe\u00e6t ure \u00e6ghwylc on o\u00f0res god\nEac swylce we sceolon \u00feysne cwide swa ongytan, \u00fe\u00e6t we on \u00f0am gemete, \u00fee he drihten us ure synna\nAc uton nu tilian, \u00fe\u00e6t we don \u00e6fter \u00fe\u00e6re drihtenlican bisene, swa he us bebead.\nUton we \u00e6ghw\u00e6\u00f0er ge ealle are, ge ealle eadmodnysse on urum d\u00e6dum healdan and don wi\u00f0 ure \u00fea\nAnd uton forl\u00e6tan and forgeofan ealle \u00fea \u00e6f\u00f0oncan and \u00fea eornesse, \u00fee o\u00f0re men wi\u00f0 eow\nAmen, amen dico vobis: Non est servus maior domino suo, So\u00f0 is, so\u00f0 is, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow secge, cw\u00e6\u00f0 se\nEfne swa swa he cw\u00e6de: Huru ge synd \u00feonne beteran, \u00fee ic, \u00fee eower drihten and eower lareow eom.\nNu ic \u00fe\u00e6t ne forhogode, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow \u00feus mid eadmodnysse \u00feenode, \u00fe\u00e6t eower \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t ne sceal \u00e6nig\nNu ge \u00feas \u00feing witan, eadige ge beo\u00f0, gif ge heo gel\u00e6sta\u00f0.\nSo\u00f0lice \u00fea menn beo\u00f0 eadige, \u00fea \u00f0e godes bebodu gefylla\u00f0, for\u00f0an \u00f0e hi onfo\u00f0 ecere mede and ecum\nHe drihten wat, hwa his \u00e6 healde\u00f0 and hwa \u00fea begange\u00f0, swa he sylf her\u00e6fter to his apostolum be\nOn \u00f0eosum wordum se unges\u00e6liga Iudas w\u00e6s openlice oncunnen, se \u00f0e \u00feurh his inwit and \u00feurh his\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend be \u00f0am ilcan Iudan: Qui manducat mecum panem, He cw\u00e6\u00f0: Se man, se \u00f0e \u00feige\u00f0\nWa \u00f0am \u00fee \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6ne bi\u00f0 mannes sunu to dea\u00f0e geseald.\nMiccle him w\u00e6re betere, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre on \u00f0as woruld acenned ne w\u00e6re.\nEfne swa unges\u00e6liglice se ungetreowa Iudas \u00feam lareowe dea\u00f0 s\u00e6tade, swa him eall his lif to\nAmen, amen, dico vobis, quia unus ex vobis me tradet, So\u00f0 is, so\u00f0 is, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow secge, \u00fe\u00e6t eower an\nOpenlice he drihten beforan him eallum s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6tte Iudas wende, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feam h\u00e6lende bemi\u00f0en w\u00e6re,\n\u00dea locedan \u00fea discipulas him betweonan and w\u00e6ron on heora modge\u00feance swi\u00f0lice afyrhte and\nWiste he drihten ana, hwa his l\u00e6wend and myr\u00f0ra w\u00e6s, swa swa him nan \u00feing bemi\u00f0en beon m\u00e6g.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00feara discipula an ofer \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes bearm hlionigende.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fees ilca Iohannes, se \u00f0e \u00feis \u00e6fter endebyrdnysse s\u00e6ge\u00f0, lufade hine se h\u00e6lend synderlice.\n\u00dea becnade Sanctus Petrus him, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde \u00e6t \u00f0am h\u00e6lende geacsian, be hwilcum heora he \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd hi miccle ma drihtnes wordum gelyfdon, \u00feonne him sylfum, for\u00f0an heora \u00e6ghwylc be heom\nButan Iudas ana, he swigade lengest, for\u00f0an \u00fee he w\u00e6s on his wordum \u00feam o\u00f0rum swa ungelic, swa\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he Crist him to andsware: Tu dixisti, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu cw\u00e6de.\n\u00dea hlionode Sanctus Iohannes ofer \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes breost, swa ic \u00e6r s\u00e6de, acsode hine \u00fea and him to\n\u00dea andswarode him se h\u00e6lend and him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Se hit is, se \u00f0e ic \u00feysne bedeptan hlaf r\u00e6can wille.\nBestang \u00fea \u00feone hlaf, \u00fee he him on handa h\u00e6fde, on \u00fe\u00e6t sealtf\u00e6t, \u00fee him beforan stod, and \u00fea sealde\nAnd \u00e6fter \u00feam breades sticce eode him on \u00fe\u00e6t wi\u00f0erwearde deofol.\nAnd he \u00fea sona \u00feanon ut gewat, swa he sy\u00f0\u00f0an fram eallum his r\u00e6de gewiten w\u00e6s.\n\u00dea ongan he drihten heom endleofenum openlice his \u00fea halgan \u00ferowunge secgan and eall \u00fea \u00feing, \u00fee\nS\u00e6ge\u00f0 man eft to merigenne, hu \u00fe\u00e6t geworden w\u00e6re.\nAc uton nu ge\u00fe\u00e6ncan, men, be \u00f0\u00e6re bysene, \u00fee se h\u00e6lend \u00feam Scariothiscan Iudan \u00feone hlaf sealde,\nUton for\u00f0an tilian, \u00fe\u00e6t we syn cl\u00e6ne and unw\u00e6mme \u00feam to onfonne, swa swa \u00fea o\u00f0re apostolas\nGod us gefultumige, \u00fe\u00e6t we to him becuman moten, se \u00f0e leofa\u00f0 and rixa\u00f0 a on ecnysse god, Amen.",
